From ebb4db20919d44b4cba9f63c1da48a22273f5cf5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Yates <me@jyates.dev>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 10:19:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: stream: Add imported DMA-BUF frame pools

Allow a zero-copy session to back either or both of its fixed frame
pools with an imported DMA-BUF instead of kernel pages, so an exporting
device (for example an integrated GPU allocating GTT pages) becomes the
payload owner and the NHI transfers directly to and from its memory.

Ring construction and DMA path activation move from first open to the
first operation that needs them: read, write, poll, the zero-copy
enable, or the import probe. The new TBSTREAM_ZC_IMPORT ioctl must run
on an exclusively opened, never-activated device, so a pool import
always precedes ring construction and no path can carry traffic into a
partially configured pool. Receive descriptors are still fully primed
before the XDomain paths are enabled. The import is transactional: the
buffer is attached to the NHI DMA device, pinned, mapped in its fixed
direction, and flattened into per-slot frame addresses with the shared
stream-sg.h validation; on any failure every acquired object is
released in reverse order and the device is left unchanged.

Imported frames have no CPU page. They are never dma_sync_single_*()
targets - the exporter owns payload coherency - and mmap() leaves their
half of the pool mapping as an unpopulated hole. Ordinary read()/write()
are rejected while an import is configured. Because an imported TX pool
cannot be written by the kernel, CLOSE packets for such sessions use one
dedicated page-backed control frame outside the slot pool. Imported
pools last until the final close of the device, surviving suspend and
resume with the rings they back.

The ioctl requires CAP_SYS_RAWIO and the zc_diagnostic_dmabuf module
parameter while the imported-pool mode remains experimental.
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/stream.c            | 498 +++++++++++++++++++++---
 include/uapi/linux/thunderbolt-stream.h |  53 +++
 2 files changed, 506 insertions(+), 45 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/stream.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/stream.c
index 197af36b5..efb8d743e 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/stream.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/stream.c
